0..73 Comment "// Univalence at the corollas of a magma\'s signature, written by hand and"
74..116 Comment "// checked against the derived `ua[1, 4]`."
117..119 Comment "//"
120..194 Comment "// The hand definition shows what `ua` builds: reflexivity at the unit for"
195..269 Comment "// the empty shape, then one `equiv` per corolla, nested to the right. Its"
270..342 Comment "// directed twin is the same shape for flows, one `forward` per corolla."
343..345 Comment "//"
346..419 Comment "// The module states the hand path beside the derived one and checks that"
420..494 Comment "// they convert. Transport and a ride along each move the binary corolla\'s"
495..553 Comment "// boolean. A ride that would reverse the flow is refused."
554..556 Comment "//"
557..629 Comment "// - see: `pathological/higher-cells/ua-by-hand-unnatural.gandr` — the"
630..684 Comment "//   naturality `ua` checks beyond the hand definition"
685..764 Comment "// - see: `ua-corolla-strata.gandr` — the Segal certification from degree two"
765..842 Comment "// - see: Shulman, _Univalence for Inverse Diagrams and Homotopy Canonicity_,"
843..877 Comment "//   doi:10.1017/S0960129514000565"
878..946 Comment "// - see: Gratzer, Weinberger and Buchholtz, _Directed univalence in"
947..1002 Comment "//   simplicial homotopy type theory_, arXiv:2407.09146"
1004..1051 Comment "// The magma, the swap and the unit\'s identity."
